     "trench"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "The hydrosphere is all the water on Earth, in oceans, rivers, lakes, ice and underground. About 71 percent of the surface is covered by water, but most is salty. The water cycle moves water by evaporation, condensation and precipitation.\nOcean water moves as waves, tides and currents. Tides rise and fall because of the Moon's and the Sun's pull, and spring tides occur at full and new moon. Warm and cold currents change climate and fishing.\nThe ocean floor has continental shelves, slopes, deep plains and trenches. Fresh water must be saved, as only a small part is usable."
    }
